Fix rnnoise's scalar fallback path, which has never compiled.

PORTABILITY FIX -- WORTH SENDING UPSTREAM.

src/vec.h dispatches three ways: AVX/SSE2, ARM NEON, and a generic scalar
#else. Only the first two have ever been built, because until now every
platform rnnoise was compiled on matched one of them. The scalar branch does
not compile at all:

  - it includes "os_support.h", which does not exist anywhere in the rnnoise
    source tree; and
  - it calls OPUS_CLEAR(), which is not defined anywhere in the rnnoise source
    tree either.

Both are leftovers from Opus, which rnnoise vendored this code from. Opus has
os_support.h and OPUS_CLEAR; rnnoise renamed the equivalent macro to RNN_CLEAR
in src/common.h and dropped the header, but missed the scalar branch of vec.h
because nothing built it. (vec_neon.h has the same stale include, but it is
guarded by __ARM_NEON so it is only reachable on ARM, where it is presumably
also broken.)

The fix is exactly the rename that was missed. RNN_CLEAR is defined in
src/common.h, which vec.h already gets via arch.h, so no new include is needed:

    #define RNN_CLEAR(dst, n) (memset((dst), 0, (n)*sizeof(*(dst))))

This is not a ppc64le-specific change. Any architecture without an
SSE2/AVX or NEON path -- ppc64le, riscv64, s390x, mips -- hits it identically.
ppc64le is simply where somebody finally took the else branch.

